@@ -449,6 +449,10 @@ The entries below give the details; the main cases are:
 
 #### Core, performance and input
 
+  - The values and the forces of the functions of vectors and matrices (e.g. the spherical harmonics of [Q6](Q6.md), [CUSTOM](CUSTOM.md) on matrices) are copied
+    between the actions and the task manager in memory order: with many components (26 for [Q6](Q6.md)) each element was a separate cache line.
+    [Q6](Q6.md) on 1000 atoms is 17% faster. The results are identical.
+
   - Less work for every action that uses atoms at every step: the periodic boundary conditions are copied into the action only when the box changes
     (and are not recomputed when the MD code passes the same box), and constant masses and charges are copied only once.
     With 200 [DISTANCE](DISTANCE.md) the calculation is about 18% faster, with 20 [GYRATION](GYRATION.md) of 1000 atoms about 4%.
